        "title": "Cache Coherence and Memory Consistency",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "In a multi-core processor, each core has its own L1 and L2 caches. If two cores cache the same memory address and one writes to it, the other core's cached value is now stale. Cache coherence protocols solve this. Memory consistency models define when a write by one core becomes visible to others."
